{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1518717-japheth-and-lazarus","id":1518717,"title":"Japheth and Lazarus","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","World of Darkness","Vampire: The Masquerade"],"posts":[{"date":"2023-07-24T12:35:37-07:00","id":1518717,"title":"Japheth and Lazarus","content":"Hi, guys!<br /> There is a rumor that Japhet may be the same person as Lazarus. But how can he assumed the other identity? Cappadocius was still active, did he not know how many children he had?<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3792-trueann","name":"trueann","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3792_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"167"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-07-24T14:41:47-07:00","id":1518720,"title":"","content":"Cappadocius would hardly be the first person to &quot;have more children than he could keep track of.&quot;<br /> <br /> Ok he might have actually been THE first person to have more children than he could keep track of, but at the very least he wouldn't be <a href=\"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Screamin%27_Jay_Hawkins\" target=\"_blank\">the last</a>.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3201-father-enoch","name":"Father Enoch","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3201_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"285"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-07-24T14:43:29-07:00","id":1518722,"title":"","content":"It's a rumour, but no, they're not the same vampire.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b><span style=\"color:#000080\">Matthew Dawkins</span><br /> <span style=\"color:#000080\">In-House Developer for Onyx Path Publishing</span></b><br /> <br /> <i><span style=\"font-family:arial\"><b><span style=\"color:#008080\">Website: </span><a href=\"http://www.matthewdawkins.com\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#008080\">https://www.matthewdawkins.com</span></a><br /> <span style=\"color:#008080\">Patreon: </span><a href=\"https://www.patreon.com/matthewdawkins\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#008080\">https://www.patreon.com/matthewdawkins</span></a></b></span></i>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/152-the-gentleman-gamer","name":"The Gentleman Gamer","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar152_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":6,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1698"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-07-24T16:59:28-07:00","id":1518725,"title":"","content":"Officially Japheth was killed and is now a wraith. It was believed he was diablarized, but since he's a wraith he must have met Final Death in some other way. Lazarus is still an un-alive vampire and is largely serving as the head of the Hecata. There were some suggestions early in the gameline that Japheth and Lazarus were the same person (and also the Capuchin) but later it was expanded on that the Capuchin is a guise that is taken on by Japheth, Lazarus and Byzer. The three of them were all children of Cappadocius and have continued to work together.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/741-anubisxy","name":"AnubisXy","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar741_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5693"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-07-25T02:02:45-07:00","id":1518747,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>The Gentleman Gamer</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1518717-japheth-and-lazarus?p=1518722#post1518722\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">It's a rumour, but no, they're not the same vampire.</div> </div> </div> </div>Thank you, another mystery was solved.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3792-trueann","name":"trueann","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3792_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"167"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-07-26T09:01:34-07:00","id":1518827,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>trueann</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1518717-japheth-and-lazarus#post1518717\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Hi, guys!<br /> There is a rumor that Japhet may be the same person as Lazarus. But how can he assumed the other identity? Cappadocius was still active, did he not know how many children he had?</div> </div> </div> </div>It's just rumor and not been confirmed as fact and from what I've seen in the lore is that they are not the same ancient and yes Cappadocius would remember just how many childer he sired as he like the rest of his generation didn't do it often.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>&quot;Power that needs to advertise itself is already losing&quot; Grand Admiral Thrawn <br /> <br /> &quot;Coronation Starscream? This is bad comedy!&quot; Galvatron","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27361-lysander","name":"Lysander","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar27361_11.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2022"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3523"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-07-29T19:46:03-07:00","id":1519150,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>AnubisXy</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1518717-japheth-and-lazarus?p=1518725#post1518725\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Officially Japheth was killed and is now a wraith. It was believed he was diablarized, but since he's a wraith he must have met Final Death in some other way.</div> </div> </div> </div>Considering the corpse of the supposed diablerist - Claudius Giovanni - <i>was given to the Capuchin himself </i>as punishment/payment for favors, according to Clanbook: Giovanni, i'd say &quot;both&quot; is a pretty valid answer.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>AnubisXy</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1518717-japheth-and-lazarus?p=1518725#post1518725\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Lazarus is still an un-alive vampire and is largely serving as the head of the Hecata. There were some suggestions early in the gameline that Japheth and Lazarus were the same person (and also the Capuchin) but later it was expanded on that the Capuchin is a guise that is taken on by Japheth, Lazarus and Byzer. The three of them were all children of Cappadocius and have continued to work together.</div> </div> </div> </div>Yes, a pretty decent solution to some hints that were quite nonsensical as given from the get-go.\u200b","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1147-baaldam","name":"Baaldam","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1147_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4937"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-08-15T08:33:03-07:00","id":1520681,"title":"","content":"The next question is how to resolve the contradictory lore on Bysar &amp; The Monitor of Instanbul being the same kindred as according to Constaniople By Night is that Byzar was put into topor by his Childe Lady Alexia.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>&quot;Power that needs to advertise itself is already losing&quot; Grand Admiral Thrawn <br /> <br /> &quot;Coronation Starscream? This is bad comedy!&quot; Galvatron","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27361-lysander","name":"Lysander","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar27361_11.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2022"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3523"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-08-15T11:25:32-07:00","id":1520690,"title":"","content":"According to &quot;Constantinople by Night&quot;, his childe incapacitated Byzar before A.D. 196.<br /> According to &quot;Clan Novel: Cappadocian&quot;, Markus Musa Giovanni found Byzar torpid body after A.D. 1204 (and left him in place).<br /> <br /> Mahatma's bio said, Emperor Constantine forces razed Byzantium to the ground, enslaved the surviving population and declared himself ruler. Mahatma himself nearly fell into torpor from grievous wounds inflicted in a battle with Roman Cainites<br /> Alexia Theusa as per her bio forced her own sire into torpor (196) when she allied herself with Mi-ka-il and the Trinity, securing herself a place as an Imperial physician<br /> So there is a tiny little contradiction here... or... actually not necesarily<br /> Since Constantine the Great lived from 272-337<br /> Antonius bio said, around 312 he joined with Michael and Dracon to become a vampiric Trinity<br /> Back to Mahatma's bio, it is said, inste\u00edd facing the formidable trio directly, Mahatma left to gather strength and knowledge with which to combat them.<br /> Alexia as imperial physician used her position to claim the bodies of the Byzantine emperors, Embracing them and staking them, binding their souls to their bodies in order to increase the chances of her lover's soul reincarnating. While not part of the Scion families, Alexia was under the protection of the Antonian Ventrue and maintained contact with the Dream Circle under the Salubri Achmet.<br /> So, the timeline a bit lines up:<br /> <br /> 550 BC: The Cappadocian Byzar found the colony of Byzantium. Mi-ka-il, now renamed Beshter, visits the place. (as per his bio)<br /> 548 BC: Beshter establishes himself in Rome<br /> 58 BC: Beshter and the Ventrue methuselah Antonius become lovers.<br /> 85 AD: Beshter adopts the Christian religion and is baptized as Michael.<br /> 152 AD: Michael meets the Tzimisce Dracon and they become lovers.<br /> 196 AD: Alexia Theusa forced her own sire into torpor when she allied herself with Mi-ka-il and the Trinity, securing herself a place as an Imperial physician<br /> 312 AD Antonius joined with Michael and Dracon to become a vampiric Trinity &quot;officially&quot; (but technically they already were a triumvirate)<br /> 326 AD: Constantine found the New Rome on the site of Byzance (that will be later renamed Constantinople). The Trinity leaves Rome to live in the new capital.<br /> <br /> Lets stop here a bit<br /> It actually makes a total sense. Michael and his lovers got disilusioned by Rome. This is basically a fact:<br /> <br /> &quot;We leave the Eternal City because its heart has long since ceased beating. It dies \u2013 and you, the lords of a once-glorious city, hide in its shadows, lost in a maze of your own construction. When our kind looks back to these times, to the death of yet another era, they will see your accomplishments and wonder what went wrong. But never, as you conceal yourselves, will they know who was responsible, to whom praise or condemnation should be addressed. Your deeds, both great and vile, will be lost to posterity, and all they will call you will be Incognitos.\u201d \u2014 Michael's last speech to the Cainites of Rome on the eve of his departure<br /> <br /> 4th Generation methuselahs nor really make decisions overnight and as he said &quot;We leave the Eternal City because <b>its heart has long since ceased beating</b>&quot; - meaning it was a long process<br /> And back then every travel - relocating your powerbase - required time and preparation.<br /> So it makes sense, it took them more than a century to finally decide to move, make the preaprations and one night, just move.<br /> As a good Cainite move, the Trinity contacted propbably the child of the ruler of the City they decided to move and let the Child do the dirty work for them<br /> Not asked questions... and Alexia probably just anounced, my Sire went in to torpor<br /> Or actually, remember, not many knew Byzar founded the city, he woirked from behind the scenes - from his haven, he directed the city's growth, and considered himself Byzantium's shepherd. He drew the greatest artists and architects from across the known world to build Byzantium, a jewel on the road to the east. <br /> Ironically, something the Trinity found &quot;worthy&quot; to be their new home<br /> It is debatable, if the Trinity knew about Byzar or not, they just allied themselves the local important Cainite - Alexia<br /> Who - since she never really liked her sire - delt with Byzar - back then, Byzar was Intrigued with Alexia's understanding of death and her unwavering loyalty to her lost love, the Cappadocian fell in love himself and offered Alexia the gift of unlife as a means to endure the ages to await the rebirth of her lover, although he hoped that she would forget him after two or three centuries and love him instead and <i>not really helped her</i> obsession to find her lost lover and help him to reincarnate.<br /> When you are a child, and have three 4th Generation methuselahs as your allies, you confindently make your move to off your sire.<br /> Understandable<br /> <br /> Back to your quesation and the problem in hand<br /> 196 AD: Alexia Theusa forced her own sire into torpor... thats clear, not ate her, that is a fact too, just torpor and stashed him away<br /> 326 AD: Constantine found the New Rome on the site of Byzance, Mahatma himself nearly fell into torpor from grievous wounds inflicted in a battle with Roman Cainites then fled from the Trinity<br /> <br /> Markus Musa Giovanni found Byzar torpid body after A.D. 1204<br /> <br /> No contradiction here actually<br /> It was nowhere said, he <b>stayed in torpor</b> - and the Cappadicans actually had Mortis powers and Fortitude combinate diciplines to... just wake up. <br /> So he proibably just aweoke, even maybe replaced the dessicated corpse in the crypt - if Alexia even visited her sire at all - and went to travel, met Saulot, became his studend... and when Saulot left him, massacred a village<br /> When Mahatma returned to his senses and saw how far he had fallen from Saulot\u2019s teachings in only a few short hours, he sank into the earth. He lay there for many nights and heard the mourning and outrage when other mortals found the destruction he had wrought. He thought he could hear Saulot's thoughts nearby, but they were elusive and he was unsure. Slowly, gripped by ennui and self-loathing, he slipped into torpor.<br /> Mahatma dreamed of Tremere's crime of Amaranth and the Triumvirate's eventual fall \u2013 Antonius' destruction, the Dracon's departure and Michael's descent into delusion. Upon awakening, Mahatma returned to his beloved Byzantium, only to find it devastated by Crusaders and barbarians, most of its beauty stolen or destroyed.<br /> Mahatma again returned to the earth's embrace, however, he heard Saulot's voice in his dreams. Each night, the voice grew louder and more insistent, and finally it drove him from the earth.<br /> Saulot instructed him to return to the path, to regain what he had lost when Saulot left him.<br /> <br /> Saulot Diableire was 1133 - and by her Bio, Mahatma/Byzar slumbered <br /> When Markus Musa Giovanni found Byzar torpid body after A.D. 1204 he not touched it... <br /> <br /> It is easy to explain, he just spent a little off time again then awoke agian and became Monitor<br /> <br /> <br /> \u200b","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/23890-shadeprowler","name":"Shadeprowler","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar23890_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"928"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-08-15T14:43:58-07:00","id":1520707,"title":"","content":"Thanks for explaining some the confusion I had on Byzar &amp; Mahatma being the same person as I was going by old material from Children of the Night and Constantnopile by Night and hearing stuff on this board that said about them being one of the same.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>&quot;Power that needs to advertise itself is already losing&quot; Grand Admiral Thrawn <br /> <br /> &quot;Coronation Starscream? This is bad comedy!&quot; Galvatron","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27361-lysander","name":"Lysander","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar27361_11.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2022"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3523"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-08-15T22:04:16-07:00","id":1520745,"title":"","content":"They are<br /> Sorry if the explanaton was confusing, used his names interchangeably\u200b","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/23890-shadeprowler","name":"Shadeprowler","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar23890_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"928"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-08-16T09:59:59-07:00","id":1520772,"title":"","content":"No it was quite detailed on how his story got complex.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>&quot;Power that needs to advertise itself is already losing&quot; Grand Admiral Thrawn <br /> <br /> &quot;Coronation Starscream? This is bad comedy!&quot; Galvatron","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27361-lysander","name":"Lysander","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar27361_11.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2022"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3523"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}